                    },
                    {
                        "not": {
                            "flag": "vote_aboard"
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "not": {
                            "flag": "room_sat"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "text": "The packet comes round the second bend low in the water, and there are more people on the green steps than there are steps. Tull ties off, takes the satchel off his shoulder, and hands up one folded sheet before anything else, because he knows what they came down for.\n\nNobody asks him. They know better. Somebody asks him anyway.\n\n\"Paper,\" Tull says. \"I carried it. It weighs the same.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Read the sheet.",
                        "next": "the_room_sat"
                    },
                    {
