                "text": "\"Sixty,\" Tull says, before you have asked. \"Sixty for a place, food's yours, and I'll not carry livestock or anything that's still arguing.\" He coils rope while he talks, which he does whether or not there is rope to coil. \"Second and the fifth. First light. I'll want a name for the book.\"",
